  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. For the period 2022-2023 the Government of Republic of Namibia successfully submitted the following reports under Article 22 regular reporting: 
a. In 2022, Namibia submitted four (4) reports on Conventions 29, 105 and 138 ; and two(2) first reports for 189 and 190.
b. In 2023, Namibia submitted five (5) regular reports on Conventions 100, 111, 122, 189, 190. 1. The ILO facilitated the sharing and discussion of the relevant texts including reporting schedule with the tripartite partners ; and the subsequent submission of the inputs.</narrative>
   </description>
